        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In a later publication, PubMed:19438211, the authors changed the enzyme activity, the connection from a histidine nitrogen to a cysteine sulfur, and the identity of the flavin from FMN to FAD. They now believe the modification is S-(8alpha-FAD)-L-cysteine, see MOD:00152. This is a deprecated entry in RESID. It probably does not occur naturally [JSG].</rdfs:comment>
