        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">From DeltaMass: References: The conversion of glutamic acid to pyroglutamic was reported for the beta-amyloid protein. Miller et al. Arch. Biochem. Biophy. (1993) 301, 41-52 [DeltaMass]. The modification in amyloid protein is probably an artifact of treatment with strong acid under anhydrous conditions. Peptides with N-terminal glutamic acid isolated from single cells of Aplysia neurons show partial conversion to pyroglutamic acid, possibly dependent on a temperature sensitive factor [JSG].</rdfs:comment>
